WEBVTT

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.210
<b>After-Action Report</b>

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.660
<b>After-Action Report</b>

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.670
<b>1st Striking Force, 
3rd Section
Battleship Yamashiro</b>

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.380
<b>1st Striking Force, 
3rd Section
Battleship Yamashiro</b>

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.020
We can still...

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.330
We can still fight, I think...

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.140
<b><b>Torpedo Squadron 2 - </b>December Formation 
Light Cruisers Yahagi, Ooyodo 
DESDIV 2: Destroyers Kasumi, Asashimo, Kiyoshimo, and others
1st Subunit - DESDIV 17: Destroyers Isokaze, Hamakaze, Yukikaze
 2nd Subunit - DESDIV 21: Destroyers Hibiki, Hatsushimo, Shigure
3rd Subunit - DESDIV 41: Destroyers Fuyutsuki, Suzutsuki</b>

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:32.610
<b><b>Yukikaze</b></b>

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:32.610
<b><b>Shigure</b></b>

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:31.380
Yukikaze of Kure, Shigure of Sasebo...

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.100
<b>Torpedo Squadron 2</b>

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.580
Okay, see you later.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.620
Breakfast, breakfast, what's for breakfast?

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.970
Stop singing and get your food.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.890
How much rice would you like?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.560
Asashimo-san, understood.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.110
Ofuyu-san, she wants a large bowl of rice.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.240
Okay, Suzu. Got it.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.410
Thank you, Ofuyu-san.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.150
Sure thing.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.920
Thanks!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.110
Kiyo, wait!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:33.000
Hurry! Hurry!

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.300
Good morning, Shigure-san.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.680
Good morning, Suzutsuki.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.980
Wow, horse mackerel!

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:48.680
That's much better than the usual fare.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.090
Is it a special occasion?

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:55.060
No, some of the local fishermen 
donated it to the Naval District, that's all.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.890
Wasn't that nice of them?

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.650
Shigure-san, how much rice would you like?

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.220
Oh, I see.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.170
I'll take a medium bowl.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.910
Medium, right? Here you are.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.900
Oh, thank you.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.480
Shigure.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.930
We're all counting on you.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.480
Sure...

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.280
Shigure-san, don't forget about this, too.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.500
Squash, raised on my farm!

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:30.930
Simmered squash? It looks delicious.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.960
Today's breakfast really 
is something special.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.220
So the enemy comes in like this, right?

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:46.180
You dodge like this, 
then counterattack like this!

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.820
Shigure.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.150
Why don't you join us?

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.350
Thanks, Isokaze.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.660
Good morning, Shigure.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.380
Hamakaze, Isokaze, good morning.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.440
It's a good... morning, isn't it?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.560
Huh? Where's Yukikaze?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.390
Oh, she's never here at breakfast.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.610
I see.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.130
Well, we all spend the morning...

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.520
...in our own ways, after all.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.290
Are you doing okay now?

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.750
Yeah, I am.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.630
Shigure?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.470
I don't know...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:36.530
But I think I've got to go forward, 
no matter what.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.760
I...

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.380
I...

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:45.860
I won't forget.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.320
About Yamashiro or the others. I remember!

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.610
I'll never forget, even for a moment!

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:58.420
And I'm going to do what I can.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.380
That's right.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:07.460
We might... Any one of us might...

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:13.930
Sink to the bottom of the sea in battle, 
with no one there to see us...

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.760
But we want someone 
to remember us, at least.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.590
Yeah.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.480
Remember that we were here...

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.270
Remember that we did the best we could...

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.910
And if they can pass that on 
to the next generation...

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:47.640
then even if I die, that's fine by me.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:54.040
Yukikaze won't sink!

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.270
Yukikaze will never sink!

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.040
You...

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.730
No running in the hallway!

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:21.580
Attention all destroyers attached 
to Torpedo Squadron 2!

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.580
We have a message from Flagship Yahagi!

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:29.040
After breakfast, all destroyers 
attached to Torpedo Squadron 2

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.920
are to immediately report 
to the command post.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:50.980
We have very little time left.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.500
Our last operation blunted 
the force of the enemy's invasion,

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.300
but it won't be long before they
 replace their losses, rebuild,

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:04.280
then launch an invasion of the Southwest 
Islands, followed by the mainland itself.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:09.980
And in the last battle, both our Naval 
District as well as the others

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:13.070
suffered the loss of many of 
our most powerful Fleet Girls.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.510
However, Torpedo Squadron 2 still stands!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:29.700
We will walk in the footsteps of the famous 
flagship of Torpedo Squadron 2, Jintsuu,

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:33.830
as well as my sister, Noshiro.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.910
Of course, we'll be every bit 
as well-trained as they were!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:12.600
<b><b>Exercise Unit - Blue Fleet 
</b>1st Subunit - DESDIV 17: Destroyers Isokaze, Hamakaze, Yukikaze
 2nd Subunit - DESDIV 21: Destroyers Hibiki, Hatsushimo, Shigure
3rd Subunit - DESDIV 41: Destroyers Fuyutsuki, Suzutsuki</b>

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:12.600
<b><b>Exercise Unit - Red Fleet
</b>Light Cruisers Yahagi, Ooyodo 
DESDIV 2: Destroyers Kasumi, Asashimo, Kiyoshimo, 
and others</b>

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.600
Torpedo Squadron 2 will conduct exercises.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.900
All our units are being reorganized.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:23.150
<b><b>Exercise Unit - Blue Fleet 
</b>1st Subunit - DESDIV 17: Destroyers Isokaze, Hamakaze, Yukikaze
 2nd Subunit - DESDIV 21: Destroyers Hibiki, Hatsushimo, Shigure
3rd Subunit - DESDIV 41: Destroyers Fuyutsuki, Suzutsuki</b>

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:22.100
But Destroyer Divisions 17, 21, and 41 
will be designated Blue Fleet.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.160
And...

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:33.160
<b><b>Exercise Unit - Red Fleet
</b>Light Cruisers Yahagi, Ooyodo 
DESDIV 2: Destroyers Kasumi, Asashimo, Kiyoshimo, 
and others</b>

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:28.760
Yahagi-san, as well as I, Ooyodo, will be
 your opponents as Red Fleet.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:35.080
Kasumi, Asashimo, and Kiyoshimo 
will serve as Red Fleet's escort.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.860
This exercise will be done 
in the form of a live battle!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:49.320
You'll be using dummy rounds, 
but it will still be dangerous.

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.640
Exercise the utmost caution 
during the battle.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.290
If you are ruled to be 
badly damaged, or sunk,

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.310
you are to immediately 
shut down your engines.

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.110
The exercise will end for you immediately.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.120
We're not doing this for glory.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.460
We're here to protect our calm seas,

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:12.340
and the lives of everybody in our nation.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.190
For that, you need training,

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:22.630
as well as enough supplies for you 
to use your training to the fullest.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:28.220
Even as we speak, a patrol fleet 
consisting of coastal defense ships

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:32.640
is keeping the sea lanes clear, 
and bringing in supplies.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:45.400
The fuel we'll be using in this exercise 
was brought to us by their efforts!

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.530
Do not waste it!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.240
Okay!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.240
Leave it to me!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.240
Roger!

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:54.130
All Destroyer Divisions are to equip 
full rigging and dummy rounds.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:58.090
Depart for the exercise area at 1000.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:01.960
The enemy surface units won't be the only 
things hunting for you out there!

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.160
Exercise utmost caution!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.420
Roger!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.220
I can't wait!

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.260
I won't give them an easy win.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:12.360
Heh. I can't wait.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.180
Don't mess this up!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:15.730
Ofuyu-san?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.740
I'm okay, Suzu.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.360
Can I take the lead? Can I?

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.510
I can, right?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.870
Shigure, let's both do our best 
as members of Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.400
Yeah.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.880
Let's get to work, Shigure.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.310
Yeah, Hibiki, let's.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.630
Who's there?

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.340
Y-Yukikaze?

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.300
Yup!

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.390
You surprised me!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.900
Did I really?

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.380
Really?

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.980
Are you sure?

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:04.700
Shigure, let's do our best out there!

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:06.010
Of course!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.820
Shigure, do you need a kiss 
from the goddess of good luck?

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:13.630
What?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.230
Okay! There's a good luck kiss for you!

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.920
You surprised me!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.950
Okay, let's do our best!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.880
Hey, they're doing an exercise, huh?

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.010
That's every ship in Torpedo Squadron 2.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:23.390
They're going all-out, huh?

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:25.590
Yahagi's leading Red Fleet?

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:27.240
Ah, and Ooyodo, too?

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:28.860
That'll be fun to watch!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.860
Yeah.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:30.870
Tch!

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:35.910
If only my new equipment was ready, 
I could've gone with them.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.800
Don't be silly.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.390
You were hurt badly, too.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:44.420
You should just be glad your 
Fleet Girl keel wasn't broken.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.690
Yeah, I know.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:48.550
What happened was really awful,

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:53.640
but for some reason, 
I feel like I'm really lucky.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.510
Thanks to your After-Action report,

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:01.350
we were able to modernize you 
and polish your chains.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.450
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.740
Oomura's Zuiuns are participating, too.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.390
Those are training aircraft! Wow!

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.230
Okay, let's get to work!

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.920
Exercise judges, taking off!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.660
Okay, begin the exercise!

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.510
The exercise has started.

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:04.830
Roger.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:08.790
Destroyer Division 17, increase speed. 
We start with the escorts on the left.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.670
Roger.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.280
Yukikaze, roger!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:17.360
Destroyer Division 21, increase speed! 
Take out the enemy fleet!

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.400
Ура... Roger!

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.850
Shigure, roger!

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.880
They're here! They're here!

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:27.150
That's Destroyer Division 17 for you! 
They're coming in fast!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.610
Keep them at a distance! Fire!

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:36.640
Too slow!

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:44.980
Gotcha!

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:51.540
Kiyoshimo has been ruled sunk. 
Shut down your engine!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.380
Leave it to me now.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.160
Why didn't you listen?

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.660
Oh? Nicely done.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.590
Division 21, Hatsushimo, attacking!

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.650
Hibiki, engaging.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:29.710
Hatsushimo has sustained light damage, 
and Hibiki heavy damage.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.900
Take this!

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:39.560
We're pushing ahead, Yukikaze!

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:41.680
Hey, Yukikaze!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:44.430
Yuki, what are you looking at?

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.930
The sky. Watch out!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.140
What?!

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:56.440
Evasive maneuvers!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:05.270
Hamakaze, heavy damage. 
Isokaze, moderate damage!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.470
Damn it!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.710
The admiral warned you that you'd 
have additional foes beyond our fleet.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.410
Is it over?

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.380
Another two, inbound!

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:21.550
That's what...

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:23.220
...we're here for!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:24.720
Suzu!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.640
Ofuyu-san!

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.220
Red fleet aerial unit has been shot down.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.530
Okay.

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.970
Not bad...

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.680
My cannons might not be 
a match for them, but...

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.230
Now!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.100
Gure! Submarine! In the water!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.030
Preparing to fire dummy depth charges...

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:25.040
Go!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.920
Red Fleet submarines have been destroyed.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:45.470
Are you going for it?

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.480
Yuki!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.190
Gure! Let's go!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.840
Take this!

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:01.110
Fire!

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:17.420
And those are the results 
of today's exercise.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.830
Understood. Thank you, and good work.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.080
Thank you, sir!

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:26.150
Ooyodo, about Yahagi...

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:27.130
Sir?

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.860
What was the look on her face?

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.730
Well, it was...

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.280
<b>After-Action Report</b>

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.380
Torpedo Squadron 2...

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.220
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Dark Clouds</b>

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:38.280
I think it's going to rain. 
You okay, Shigure?
